{{also|rock-paper-scissors}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rock-paper-scissors}}

===Etymology===
A calque of the handshapes in Japanese [[janken]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|games}} A popular children's [[game]] using three [[hand]] [[sign]]s representing rock, paper and scissors, frequently used as a [[tiebreaker]].
# By extension, any situation where strategies are not [[transitive]], meaning each strategy is strong against some strategies and weak against others in a loop such that there is no universally best option.

